res and renovation of our hotels could materially and adversely affect our financial condition and results of operations.","block":206,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-011060","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-24","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001616000","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1616000/000162828026011060/xhr-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/3b588e54d101c599dcdd2416f5d2289e5d865228307802bfafaadb6dd5ff4ab0.bin","sha256":"3b588e54d101c599dcdd2416f5d2289e5d865228307802bfafaadb6dd5ff4ab0"}},{"id":"54e11320f5ef9cdf22e613f64ab8bc4700ae6fa1553948235920f64c41609155","quote":"•If third-party hotel managers and/or franchisors consolidate through merger and acquisition transactions, we may experience undefined and unknown costs related to the integration of processes and systems.","context":"•Contractual and other disagreements with or involving third-party hotel management companies and franchisors could make us liable to them or result in litigation costs or other expenses.","section":"•Any difficulties in obtaining capital necessary to make required periodic capital expenditures and renovation of our hotels could materially and adversely affect our financial condition and results of operations.","block":207,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-011060","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-24","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001616000","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1616000/000162828026011060/xhr-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/3b588e54d101c599dcdd2416f5d2289e5d865228307802bfafaadb6dd5ff4ab0.bin","sha256":"3b588e54d101c599dcdd2416f5d2289e5d865228307802bfafaadb6dd5ff4ab0"}},{"id":"fa868368cf41a9db307968fd1d49dfe382c8fd2ee71048e1e45ee40f6b035a26","quote":"•If we were to lose a brand license at one or more of our hotels, the value of the affected hotels could decline significantly and we could incur significant costs to obtain new franchise licenses.","context":"•If third-party hotel managers and/or franchisors consolidate through merger and acquisition transactions, we may experience undefined and unknown costs related to the integration of processes and systems.","section":"•Any difficulties in obtaining capital necessary to make required periodic capital expenditures and renovation of our hotels could materially and adversely affect our financial condition and results of operations.","block":208,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-011060","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-24","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001616000","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1616000/000162828026011060/xhr-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/3b588e54d101c599dcdd2416f5d2289e5d865228307802bfafaadb6dd5ff4ab0.bin","sha256":"3b588e54d101c599dcdd2416f5d2289e5d865228307802bfafaadb6dd5ff4ab0"}},{"id":"17cc7658790d9204c31d63499436f956fb5f6745d47a8e7f6e4b1076ad9c91d4","quote":"•Volatility in the financial markets and challenging economic conditions could adversely affect our ability to secure debt financing on attractive terms and our ability to service any future indebtedness that we may incur.","context":"•If we were to lose a brand license at one or more of our hotels, the value of the affected hotels could decline significantly and we could incur significant costs to obtain new franchise licenses.","section":"•Any difficulties in obtaining capital necessary to make required periodic capital expenditures and renovation of our hotels could materially and adversely affect our financial condition and results of operations.","block":209,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-011060","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-24","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001616000","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1616000/000162828026011060/xhr-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/3b588e54d101c599dcdd2416f5d2289e5d865228307802bfafaadb6dd5ff4ab0.bin","sha256":"3b588e54d101c599dcdd2416f5d2289e5d865228307802bfafaadb6dd5ff4ab0"}},{"id":"06c56057408875e39ce63a907bd8d28a96abfb23ea54fd53d7e03f31a6245aa6","quote":"•Our organizational documents have no limitation on the amount of indebtedness we may incur. As a result, we may become highly leveraged in the future, which could materially and adversely affect us.","context":"•Volatility in the financial markets and challenging economic conditions could adversely affect our ability to secure debt financing on attractive terms and our ability to service any future indebtedness that we may incur.","section":"•Any difficulties in obtaining capital necessary to make required periodic capital expenditures and renovation of our hotels could materially and adversely affect our financial condition and results of operations.","block":210,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-011060","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-24","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001616000","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1616000/000162828026011060/xhr-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/3b588e54d101c599dcdd2416f5d2289e5d865228307802bfafaadb6dd5ff4ab0.bin","sha256":"3b588e54d101c599dcdd2416f5d2289e5d865228307802bfafaadb6dd5ff4ab0"}},{"id":"5a493755445784dbd18dcfa090457c8479fdd310018d3e598fa7bfccaf371c27","quote":"•If we are unable to repay or refinance our existing debt, we may be unable to reinstate or increase distributions to our stockholders and our share price may be adversely affected.","context":"8","section":"•Any difficulties in obtaining capital necessary to make required periodic capital expenditures and renovation of our hotels could materially and adversely affect our financial condition and results of operations.","block":212,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-011060","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-24","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001616000","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1616000/000162828026011060/xhr-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/3b588e54d101c599dcdd2416f5d2289e5d865228307802bfafaadb6dd5ff4ab0.bin","sha256":"3b588e54d101c599dcdd2416f5d2289e5d865228307802bfafaadb6dd5ff4ab0"}},{"id":"50f120791d9ff92747a2fff0806a0466394e47ca123085135a776fbed0653459","quote":"•Covenants applicable to current or future debt could restrict our ability to make distributions to our stockholders and, as a result, we may be unable to make distributions necessary to qualify as a REIT.","context":"•If we are unable to repay or refinance our existing debt, we may be unable to reinstate or increase distributions to our stockholders and our share price may be adversely affected.","section":"•Any difficulties in obtaining capital necessary to make required periodic capital expenditures and renovation of our hotels could materially and adversely affect our financial condition and results of operations.","block":213,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-011060","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-24","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001616000","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1616000/000162828026011060/xhr-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/3b588e54d101c599dcdd2416f5d2289e5d865228307802bfafaadb6dd5ff4ab0.bin","sha256":"3b588e54d101c599dcdd2416f5d2289e5d865228307802bfafaadb6dd5ff4ab0"}},{"id":"0f5f96100d58d5e6e19268a55714745bcc559a3f7bd158b090637fdb60e351ff","quote":"•We may be contractually obligated to purchase property even if we are unable to secure financing for the acquisition.","context":"•Covenants applicable to curren